k profile linked for activate_destination_node and for lock? lock does not need task profile. But to mark dispatch ready we need transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized (which need candidate_task_profile_linked? Actually authorize_transport_leg_loading requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. So origin_availability_alpha needs task profile linked for authorize. Similarly destination? The authorize action uses origin_availability only; destination not needed. But to mark destination dispatch ready we need transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized (same). So destination does not need its own task profile link for those actions. However activate_destination_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?destination_availability ?route_task_profile. So destination also needs task profile linked.

